    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "History",
            "paragraphs": [
                "St Alban's was built for the working class who lived in the Thornton Heath /Selhurst areas.\nWe are not entirely sure where the money came from to build the church but we do know it was built in stages depending on whether the funds were available or not. This had a profound influence  on whether the  original plans were followed,  scaled down or  discarded and new plans drawn up.",
                ""
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Focus of the Open Day",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The focus of the Open Day will be to empathise with the architect and builders as the church began to take shape and the challenges faced and how they were overcome. \n We will also celebrate the role that St Alban's has played since 1891 within the community."
            ]
        }
    ],
